# Build trees
build/
build-*/
build32/
compile_commands.json
*.o
*.so
*.spv

# IDE / OS
.cache/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.user
.DS_Store

# makepkg works in the packaging directory and leaves its results there. The
# packages themselves are build output like any other: 120 MB of them had
# accumulated beside the PKGBUILD before this line existed.
packaging/pkg/
packaging/src/
packaging/*.pkg.tar.*
# A VCS source is cached as a bare clone named after it, beside the PKGBUILD.
# Found by running the public PKGBUILD for the first time: two of them appeared
# as untracked directories in a repository that had just been published.
packaging/vocem-overlay/
packaging/imgui/

# Python leaves these beside any script it IMPORTS rather than runs, which is
# how a 24 KB .pyc of rpc-probe.py came to sit untracked in scripts/ -- one
# `git add -A` from a compiled binary in a public repository.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Fetched by scripts/make-fonts.py, which deletes them again; what is committed
# is the subsets it produces under common/fonts/.
third_party/fonts/*-Variable.ttf
# Two of the six are not named "-Variable": the pattern above was written when
# there were three fonts, and NotoSansMath-Regular.ttf and
# NotoSansSymbols2-Regular.ttf fell outside it. The script unlinks all six in
# a `finally` now (entry 182); these two lines are for a run killed before it
# gets there.
third_party/fonts/NotoSansMath-Regular.ttf
third_party/fonts/NotoSansSymbols2-Regular.ttf

# AI tooling
.claude/
CLAUDE.md
DESIGN.md
PROMPT-*.md
AUDIT-*.md

# flatpak-builder leaves its cache and its build trees beside the manifest.
.flatpak-builder/
# And the release build keeps its build directory and its exported repository
# there too, deliberately: all three have to be on one filesystem, and /tmp on
# this machine is a tmpfs the builder's sandbox does not even share. See
# flatpak/README.md.
vocem-flatpak-build/
vocem-flatpak-repo/
